module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.record_field_admits_a_distinct_product_value

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data record_field_admits_a_distinct_product_value: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "record_field_admits_a_distinct_product_value" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a record literal's field declared as one nominal product is initialised with a NON-LITERAL value of a DISTINCT product, and the program is Accepted. HARM: silent wrongness at the compiler floor -- DESIGN section 4b names `values inhabit declared types` as part of the ordinary floor, so this is below it, not a rung.",

    "SPECIMEN, measured on main 7af52ea7e2 with an entry compile (`gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <probe> --target dag`): `type RfA { a: Int }`, `type RfB { b: String }`, `type RfHolderB { f: RfB }`, `fn rf_a() -> RfA { RfA { a: 1 } }`, `fn rf_field_distinct_product() -> RfHolderB { RfHolderB { f: rf_a() } }` -- ACCEPTED, no diagnostic at the field. The probe is not enrolled: an expected-red claim needs a roster row in the floor's expected-red authority, and this row records the specimen source here instead so it can be re-run verbatim.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, from the same compile. (1) The SAME value at a call argument -- `fn rf_take_b(x: RfB) -> RfB`, `rf_take_b(x: rf_a())` -- REFUSES `value does not inhabit its declared type at the direct call argument`, through v1.compiler.infer nominal_product_inhabitance_refusal. (2) A record LITERAL of the distinct product at the same field -- `RfHolderB { f: RfA { a: 1 } }` -- REFUSES `type mismatch`, through structured_application_site_type_mismatch, which judges only an actual whose EXPRESSION is a record literal. (3) So the gap is the non-literal value at the record-field position: that position's judgment in infer_record_lit_structural is a local chain (kernel mismatch, structured literal, coproduct payload at parent) that never consults the nominal-product relation the call-argument and declared-return positions share. The obligation itself exists: infer_record_lit_structural constructs a DeclaredTypeObligation at PositionRecordLiteralField, but only for the cardinality verdict (optional_at_required_value_obligation_diags); the nominal-product inhabitance judgment never consumes it.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder (silently wrong). CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- both identities are established and the relation that decides them exists. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as the capability: field-value inhabitance judged by declared product identity at the record-field position, through the same nominal-product relation the call-argument position consumes, not a per-site guard. SUFFICIENT FOR: the specimen above to refuse, located at the field value, while a value of the declared product and a transparent alias of it stay accepted. OWNER: none yet.",

    "SEED REPAIR (gunbc#13226): the earliest unjustified boundary was the field seam itself -- both identities are established upstream and the deciding relation existed; v1.compiler.infer infer_record_lit_structural simply never consulted it. It now consumes nominal_product_inhabitance_refusal and refuses DeclaredTypeNotInhabited located at the field value, for record and variant fields, judging an optional field against its required element. v2 was never in the class: v2.compiler.infer hands each field value to v2.std.inhabitance declared_type_inhabitance under position_record_field. CORPUS CENSUS, from the required floor on that PR's first head (2579 modules resolved): two newly refused sites, both in gunbc.scm.checkout checkout_repository_at, each placing a RepositoryManifestRoot in CheckoutWouldDiscardStagedWork.candidate declared CorpusManifestObjectRef -- a real defect, repaired by projecting the root's own `root` field, not a conversion. FIXTURE: test.claim.record_field_distinct_product_witness, four reds and five controls. RUNG, at the grain the relation claims and no wider: structurally guaranteed for a concrete named product (or its transparent alias) at a record or variant field on the seed path. Everything outside that grain is a stated residual in the next receipt.",

    "RESIDUALS AT THE RECORD-FIELD POSITION AFTER THE SEED REPAIR, each read off the relation's own guards and NOT yet measured by a probe, each with its own next-rung trigger. (1) A FIELD OF A GENERIC OWNER WITH AN UNBOUND PARAMETER, which includes a value the author wraps as `Present { value: x }` for a `B?` field: infer_record_lit_structural returns no diagnostics when direct_call_formal_has_unbound_type_variable holds for the field type. TRIGGER: the field obligation judged under the owner's instantiation from the expected type. (2) ZERO-FIELD PRODUCTS, ANONYMOUS RECORDS AND CALLABLES: nominal_product_head_name answers no head for them, the limit nominal_product_inhabitance_refusal declares for every position it serves. TRIGGER: that relation establishes those heads, which climbs the call-argument and declared-return positions with this one. (3) WHERE-REFINEMENT BRAND NARROWING: a refinement is excluded from the nominal-product arm and this position does not consult refinement_inhabitance, so a base value at a brand-typed field is unjudged and no brand wall at a field is established. TRIGGER: refinement_inhabitance decides narrowing as a refusal and the field position consumes it. (4) THE POSITION AS A WHOLE: it runs two verdicts of the relation, not the relation. TRIGGER: the field hands its obligation to declared_type_obligation_diags after the older chain is measured against it on the corpus, which deletes that chain and subsumes (2) and (3) at this position.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
